---
import { SOCIAL } from '../consts';

/**
 * "Say something" — the tilted grid floor and horizon line.
 *
 * The location is deliberately not a real one. The mockup's `SEATTLE ·
 * 47.6°N 122.3°W` was dropped (a home city is its owner's call, not a
 * mockup's) and replaced with an Easter egg that keeps the *form* of a
 * location line while pointing somewhere else entirely.
 *
 * 43.3°S 11.4°W is the genuine selenographic position of Tycho crater on the
 * Moon — the TMA-1 excavation site in 2001: A Space Odyssey. The coordinates
 * are real and check out; they are simply not on this planet. It also happens
 * to be the one choice that honours the mockup's own note that this world is
 * "vacuum, not street", which is why the page has a star field and no rain.
 *
 * The mockup's `matthew@memerson.com` is still omitted — it is not
 * corroborated anywhere in this repo and an unverified address invites
 * bounced mail. See docs/UI-DESIGN.md §8.
 */
---

<footer class="foot">
  <div class="foot-floor" data-fx="tilt" aria-hidden="true"></div>
  <div class="foot-horizon" aria-hidden="true"></div>
  <div class="foot-body">
    <span class="foot-title">Say something</span>
    <span class="foot-links">
      <a href={SOCIAL.github}>GITHUB ↗</a>
      <a href={SOCIAL.linkedin}>LINKEDIN ↗</a>
      <a href="/rss.xml">RSS ↗</a>
    </span>
    <span class="foot-note">TYCHO · LUNA · 43.3°S 11.4°W</span>
  </div>
</footer>
